r they kiss  their wives and they kiss their little  children and they turn right around and  volunteered to the military these were  not soldiers these are businessmen these  are attorneys with no military  experience they had some cursory  training and they took off their  shoulder pads and put on camouflage and  started fighting the Russians and for  eight months I have corresponded with  them much like you would in the olden  days as pen pals I would send them a  video they would send me a video me for  my couch them from in front of a blown  out building and you will not believe  the place The Story Goes this um it's  the most important most powerful and  most painful thing I've ever been  involved with it's amazing what's  amazing about this documentary is it  takes you inside the fox I mean we're we  often see videos from Ukraine from  surveillance cameras and things like  that but it's so up close and personal  and the title who if not us where did  that title come from that's their Creed  that is the translation of a Ukrainian  phrase saying we have to do this this is  the only way we're going to do this no  one else we are outnumbered we are  outmanned we are outgunned and if we  were to stay with our families our  country would be taken over and the  access is unbelievable from the Foxhole  you mentioned there are so many sobering  moments you have with these men I  remember when I was speaking to Yuri who  is the president of the Ukrainian League  of American football and he said I'm a  soldier I'm not afraid of gunfire that's  what I do I'm not afraid of a battle I'm  not afraid of an eye to eye combat what  I'm afraid of is I'm killed in my sleep  by a rocket and I never had a chance to  fight that is some of the things we have  here and you know Nate it's there's  there's a Bedrock of football through it  too and teammates and the lessons  learned and all of those things and  there's levity but it's an unbelievably  sobering thing that I just still can't  believe I was involved with it well you  said something that sort of jumped out  at me Kyle you talked about  corresponding with them from the comfort  of your couch and even as journalists  who are covering this conflict this war  in Ukraine ultimately they get to go  home vast majority of them the men and  women that are fighting this aggression  from Russia have to stay there it is  their home you spoke though to Yuri's  wife they are now refugees living in  Latvia with their uh with her young  daughter their young daughter what did  they tell you about what life is like  there  it's difficult I'm glad you know this I  felt part of the story was I have to do  the best I can to get my hands dirty and  I got to get out of the suburbs and I  got to get out of the cul-de-sac and I  got to get as close as I can I went to  Latvia I went to Poland and that's where  they're living and I met with the wives  and this is me seeing Yuri for the first  time uh in a park in Riga Latvia and to  sit down with these unbelievably  powerful women and hear their messages I  asked one of them I said I'm trying so  hard we all are in the United States to  relate what you might be going through  when you fled in that moment when your  husband said goodbye and you don't know  when you're going to see them or if  you're going to see them do you not  plead with him and say your place is  with us your place is taking care of us  this is this is your responsibility do  you not try to beg him to stay with us  and she said of course not no I would  never my husband is a hero and heroes  fight I would never deprive him of that  and I get goosebumps talking about it  right now I I will never forget it and  that's how powerful those women are  um October 19th was an emotional day for  you Danilo who was one of the players  one of the fighters one of the heroes  was killed in battle and he told you he  said no I don't want to be forgotten  what did he stand for  tinilo stood for everything this cost  stands for there are there are four  gentlemen who I became friends with I  care about these people a lot and this  is after six months of fighting and I  get a message on my phone it's 1 30 p.m  on a Wednesday and I'm doing dishes and  the text was when one of our producers  in NFL 360 that said Danilo has been  killed what's particularly painful about  this is that Danilo was fighting with  his brother this is a video here where  Danilo finds out he was going to be an  uncle for the first time Danilo and  Roman were brothers and not only were  they Brothers they were teammates they  were in the same backfield one was a  fullback one was the tailback they  enlisted together and they decided to  fight separately because they didn't  want their love for each other to be  distracted from their cause  Danilo was in the southern Ukrainian  city of Curson and he was killed when he  left cover to help a comrade and less  than 48 hours I spoke with his brother  Roman as part of this piece and it again  is something I will never forget do his  family members regret him doing this I  know you talked about Yuri's wife saying  she doesn't want to deprive him of  his right to defend his country but I  wonder when you lose somebody do you  then say you know maybe we shouldn't  have gotten involved I thought the same  thing and not for a second yeah they  would change nothing I figured you'd say  that I spoke to Rome and his brother and  I said how do you feel after this same  thing would you have gone back  differently  this man said to me my only fear in this  war the only thing I'm afraid of is  something happening to my brother  and now that my brother's gone I have no  fear there's nothing I'm afraid of and  he has said  now they can't touch me and now I'm even  more powerful and um  very very powerful man I am looking  forward to this thank you for coming and  joining us  um and thank you for your work you know  you have a million jobs you work like I  do you also our husband father coach so  I'm doing an assignment like this I know  it's tough but we appreciate it because  these are the stories we need to hear  when it comes to this fight in Ukraine  Kyle Grant we appreciate you you can see  the NFL 360 documentary who if not us at  8pm tonight on NFL Network
 

